{
 "id": "lem-sfb-bochner-integral-subtraction",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Subtraction and almost-everywhere congruence for complex integrals",
 "statement": "Use $\\mathbf R,\\mathbf C$ [def-weil-field]. Let $(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $f,g:X\\to\\mathbf C$ be Lebesgue integrable. Then $$\\int_X(f-g)\\,d\\mu=\\int_X f\\,d\\mu-\\int_X g\\,d\\mu.$$ For arbitrary $f,g:X\\to\\mathbf C$ with $f=g$ almost everywhere, their Bochner integrals agree (using the convention that the integral is zero when the function is not integrable).",
 "source": {
